  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A plane polarized blue light ray is incident on a prism such that there is no reflection from the surface of the prism. The angle of deviation of the emergent ray is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#948;</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>60</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup></math> (see Figure-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>). The angle of minimum deviation for red light from the same prism is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#948;</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>30</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup></math> (see Figure-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>). The refractive index of the prism material for blue light is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>. Which of the following statement(s) is(are) correct?</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0007_5fce120cdc5f.png\" style=\"width: 600px; height: 184px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "The blue light is polarized in the plane of incidence",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "The angle of the prism is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>45</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "The refractive index of the material of the prism for red light is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "The angle of refraction for blue light in air at the exit plane of the prism is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>60</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A",
    "C",
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For no reflection:</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0007_18ff728be31e.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 242px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p>Applying Snell&#39;s law at left interface, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>30</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup></math></p><p>Now, for given values</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#948;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>A</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>A</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi></math></p><p>Then,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>30</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup></math></p><p>For red light:</p><p>Expression to find minimum deviation is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>&#948;</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math></p>"
  }
}